{%- comment -%}
  snippets/ds-cart-summary.liquid — Disrupted Studio cart drawer footer

  Renders the bottom of the cart drawer: total (subtotal/discount
  breakdown only shown when a discount is applied), checkout button,
  express checkout buttons, taxes/license note.

  Cart-level discounts use Shopify's `cart.cart_level_discount_applications`
  (auto-applied via discount codes or scripts). Line-level discounts are
  already reflected in line `final_price` so they don't need a separate row.

  License-terms consent: the old click-wrap checkbox was removed in
  favor of a "by purchasing you agree" line in the note below + matching
  language on /pages/license. Purchase-as-acceptance is industry-standard
  for digital goods (Pangram, Hvnter, Klim all use it).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # Show the Subtotal + per-discount breakdown only when a cart-level
  # discount is actually in play. For the common case (no discount),
  # subtotal === total === total_price minus tax (added at checkout),
  # so a separate Subtotal row would just be visual noise.
  assign has_discount = false
  if cart.original_total_price > cart.total_price
    assign has_discount = true
  endif
-%}

<div class="ds-cart__summary">
  <div class="ds-cart__summary-rows">
    {%- if has_discount -%}
      <div class="ds-cart__sub-row">
        <span class="ds-cart__sub-label">Subtotal</span>
        <span class="ds-cart__sub-value">
          <text-component value="{{ cart.original_total_price | money | strip_html }}">
            {{ cart.original_total_price | money }}
          </text-component>
        </span>
      </div>

      {%- for discount in cart.cart_level_discount_applications -%}
        <div class="ds-cart__sub-row ds-cart__sub-row--discount">
          <span class="ds-cart__sub-label">{{ discount.title }}</span>
          <span class="ds-cart__sub-value">−{{ discount.total_allocated_amount | money }}</span>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="ds-cart__sub-row ds-cart__sub-row--total">
      <span class="ds-cart__sub-label">Total</span>
      <span class="ds-cart__sub-value">
        <text-component value="{{ cart.total_price | money_with_currency | strip_html }}">
          {{ cart.total_price | money_with_currency }}
        </text-component>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <form
    action="{{ routes.cart_url }}"
    method="post"
    id="cart-checkout-form"
    class="ds-cart__checkout-form"
    novalidate
  >
    <button
      type="submit"
      name="checkout"
      class="ds-btn ds-btn--lg ds-btn--accent ds-cart__checkout-btn"
    >
      Checkout — {{ cart.total_price | money }}
    </button>

    {%- comment -%}
      Accelerated / express checkout buttons (Shop Pay, PayPal, Apple
      Pay, Google Pay) — Shopify renders whichever ones the merchant
      has enabled in Settings → Payments → Express checkouts. The
      `additional_checkout_buttons` variable is only true when at
      least one is configured, so on stores without these enabled
      this section emits nothing.

      Shop Pay's web component handles its own click → token →
      checkout flow; we don't need our own form submission for it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if additional_checkout_buttons -%}
      <div class="ds-cart__express">
        {{ content_for_additional_checkout_buttons }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </form>

  {%- comment -%}
    Tight single-line (wraps to two on narrow viewports) of footer
    info — tax, delivery, license link. Each item is a span so the
    flex container can space + wrap them cleanly. The license link
    is the consent surface; purchase-as-acceptance is documented on
    /pages/license itself.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="ds-cart__note">
    <span>Tax at checkout</span>
    <span class="ds-cart__note-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
    <span>Instant download</span>
    <span class="ds-cart__note-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
    <a href="/pages/license" class="ds-cart__note-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">License terms</a>
  </p>
</div>
